  "claim": "The actress who had the role of Summer Shaw in the soap opera \"Hollyoaks\" played Meg Giry in a musical written by this English comedian, author, playwright, actor, and director. He is also the writer of \"The Young Ones\". The musical was composed by Charles Hart with lyrics by Glenn Slater.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Ben Elton. Sentence: Benjamin Charles Elton (born 3 May 1959) is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor and director.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: He was a part of London's alternative comedy movement of the 1980s and became a writer on series such as \"The Young Ones\" and \"Blackadder\", as well as continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: Since then he has published 15 novels and written the musicals \"We Will Rock You\" (2002) and \"Love Never Dies\" (2010), the sequel to \"The Phantom of the Opera\".\nPage: Love Never Dies (musical). Sentence: Love Never Dies is a romantic musical composed by Andrew Lloyd Webber with lyrics by Glenn Slater and a book by Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth and Slater.\nPage: Summer Strallen. Sentence: Her most notable theatre credits include Meg Giry in the West End production of \"Love Never Dies\" and Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of \"The Sound of Music\" at the London Palladium.\nPage: Summer Shaw. Sentence: Summer Shaw is a fictional character from the British Channel 4 soap opera, \"Hollyoaks\", played by Summer Strallen.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Ben Elton. Sentence: Benjamin Charles Elton (born 3 May 1959) is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor and director.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: He was a part of London's alternative comedy movement of the 1980s and became a writer on series such as \"The Young Ones\" and \"Blackadder\", as well as continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: Since then he has published 15 novels and written the musicals \"We Will Rock You\" (2002) and \"Love Never Dies\" (2010), the sequel to \"The Phantom of the Opera\".\nPage: Love Never Dies (musical). Sentence: Love Never Dies is a romantic musical composed by Andrew Lloyd Webber with lyrics by Glenn Slater and a book by Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth and Slater.\nPage: Summer Strallen. Sentence: Her most notable theatre credits include Meg Giry in the West End production of \"Love Never Dies\" and Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of \"The Sound of Music\" at the London Palladium.\nPage: Summer Shaw. Sentence: Summer Shaw is a fictional character from the British Channel 4 soap opera, \"Hollyoaks\", played by Summer Strallen.",
